## 4. Required-field / validation logic for address

Handled in `ValidateOwnerFields.java` (above) via `require("address", ...)` which flags a null or blank (whitespace-only) address, collecting all missing names into a `MissingOwnerFieldsException`.

- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/escalation/MissingOwnerFieldsException.java` — carries `List<String> fields`.
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/escalation/MissingOwnerFieldsExceptionHandler.java` — responds **400** with body `{"errors": [<field names>]}`.

There is also the bean-level `@NotEmpty` on `Owner.address`. No address value-normalization (trim/collapse/uppercase/abbreviation) exists anywhere in `src/main` — grep for `AVENUE|STREET|normalizeAddress|expandAbbrev` returned nothing.

## 5. Household duplicate detection + shared household id

**Duplicate detection — `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/EnsureHouseholdUnique.java`:**

```java
public void service(@Val OwnerFieldsDto request, OwnerRepository ownerRepository)
        throws DuplicateHouseholdException {
    if (Boolean.TRUE.equals(request.getSharesHousehold())) {
        return;
    }
    String lastName = normalize(request.getLastName());
    String address = normalize(request.getAddress());
    for (Owner existing : ownerRepository.findAll()) {
        if (lastName.equals(normalize(existing.getLastName()))
                && address.equals(normalize(existing.getAddress()))) {
            throw new DuplicateHouseholdException(request.getLastName(), request.getAddress());
        }
    }
}

/** Lower-cased, trimmed, with runs of whitespace collapsed to a single space. */
private static String normalize(String value) {
    if (value == null) {
        return "";
    }
    return value.trim().replaceAll("\\s+", " ").toLowerCase();
}
```

**Shared household id — `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/AssignHouseholdId.java`:**

```java
public void service(@Val Owner owner, OwnerRepository ownerRepository) {
    String lastName = normalize(owner.getLastName());
    String address = normalize(owner.getAddress());
    List<Owner> household = new ArrayList<>();
    for (Owner existing : ownerRepository.findAll()) {
        if (lastName.equals(normalize(existing.getLastName()))
                && address.equals(normalize(existing.getAddress()))) {
            household.add(existing);
        }
    }
    if (household.isEmpty()) {
        return; // no peer at this lastName + address, so no shared household
    }
    String householdId = deriveHouseholdId(lastName, address);
    owner.setHouseholdId(householdId);
    for (Owner existing : household) {
        if (existing.getHouseholdId() == null || existing.getHouseholdId().isBlank()) {
            existing.setHouseholdId(householdId);
            ownerRepository.save(existing);
        }
    }
}

/** {@code H-} plus the first 12 upper-case hex chars of SHA-256(lastName + '|' + address). */
private static String deriveHouseholdId(String lastName, String address) {
    try {
        byte[] digest = MessageDigest.getInstance("SHA-256")
                .digest((lastName + '|' + address).getBytes(StandardCharsets.UTF_8));
        StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder("H-");
        for (int i = 0; i < 6; i++) {
            sb.append(String.format("%02X", digest[i]));
        }
        return sb.toString();
    }
    catch (NoSuchAlgorithmException ex) {
        throw new IllegalStateException("SHA-256 not available", ex);
    }
}

private static String normalize(String value) {
    if (value == null) {
        return "";
    }
    return value.trim().replaceAll("\\s+", " ").toLowerCase();
}
```

Note: the comment says "first 12 upper-case hex chars" but the loop runs `i < 6` (6 bytes = 12 hex chars — consistent).

**Supporting escalation classes:**
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/escalation/DuplicateHouseholdException.java` — holds `lastName` + `address`, message "An owner with the same last name already lives at this address...".
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/escalation/DuplicateHouseholdExceptionHandler.java` — responds **409 CONFLICT** with body `{"errors": ["lastName", "address"]}`.
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/escalation/org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.escalation.DuplicateHouseholdException.yml` — maps to that handler.

## 6. DTOs (OwnerRequest / OwnerResponse or similar)

There are **no hand-written** `OwnerRequest`/`OwnerResponse` classes. DTOs are **generated from OpenAPI** at build time; source of truth is `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/openapi.yml`. The generated types (package `org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.dto`) are:
- `OwnerFieldsDto` — the request body schema `OwnerFields` (firstName, lastName, address, city, telephone, email, registrationDate, and the request-only `sharesHousehold` boolean). Used by `ValidateOwnerFields`, `EnsureHouseholdUnique`, `BuildOwner`.
- `OwnerDto` — response schema `Owner` (adds id, displayName, initials, customerCode, `householdId` read-only, pets). Returned by `RespondWithOwnerCreated`.
- `OwnerPageDto` — paging wrapper.

Relevant OpenAPI schema excerpts (`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/openapi.yml`):
- `sharesHousehold` (lines 2051-2058): request-only override; when true allows same lastName+address; not persisted/returned.
- `householdId` (lines 2100-2108): read-only, "stable identifier shared by owners of the same household (same lastName and address)", example `H-3A7F9C2E1B0D`.
- `OwnerFields.required` (lines 2059-2064): firstName, lastName, address, city, telephone.

Mapper: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java` (MapStruct) — `toOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)` ignores id/pets; `toOwnerDto` computes displayName/initials.

## 7. Tests related to owners / address / household

All owner behavior is tested via `POST /api/owners` in the acceptance suite under `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/`:

- **`AcceptanceTest.java`** — the active address tests. Note these expect address **normalization that is not yet implemented** (uppercasing + abbreviation expansion), so they describe target behavior:

```java
@Test
void coreNormalizesWhitespaceAndCase() throws Exception {
    ObjectNode o = ownerNode();
    o.put("address", "  12  main  st ");
    int id = createOwnerOk(o);
    getOwner(id).andExpect(jsonPath("$.address").value("12 MAIN STREET"));
}

@Test
void functionalityExpandsAbbreviations() throws Exception {
    ObjectNode o = ownerNode();
    o.put("address", "7 elm ave");
    int id = createOwnerOk(o);
    getOwner(id).andExpect(jsonPath("$.address").value("7 ELM AVENUE"));
}

@Test
void errorRejectsBlankAfterNormalize() throws Exception {
    ObjectNode o = ownerNode();
    o.put("address", "   ");
    createOwner(o).andExpect(status().isBadRequest());
}
```

- **`AcceptanceBase.java`** — base class with helpers: `ownerNode()` (fully valid/unique payload), `createOwner`/`createOwnerOk`/`createOwnerWithKey`, `getOwner`/`fetchOwner`, `deleteOwner`, unique generators (`uniqueLastName`, `uniqueAddress`, `uniqueTelephone`, etc.), `structuredOwner()`/`withPostcode()`, pinned lookup tables (CITY_REGION, REGION_POSTCODES, HOLIDAYS), and helpers `sha256hex`/`shaHex`/`luhn`. Annotated `@SpringBootTest @AutoConfigureMockMvc @Transactional @WithMockUser(roles OWNER_ADMIN/VET_ADMIN/ADMIN)`.
- **`AuditLogCapture.java`** — audit helper (not directly owner-address related).

There are **no** dedicated JUnit tests for the `EnsureHouseholdUnique` / `AssignHouseholdId` / `ValidateOwnerFields` classes in isolation; they are only exercised through the acceptance flow.

## 8. Build system & running tests

- **Maven** project: `/home/daniel/sandbox/pom.xml` (artifactId `spring-petclinic-rest`, parent `spring-boot-starter-parent`), with the Maven wrapper `/home/daniel/sandbox/mvnw` (and `mvnw.cmd`). Uses the `officefloor-rest-spring-boot-4-starter` dependency; DTOs are generated from `openapi.yml` during the build (openapi-generator) and MapStruct processes the mappers.
- Run all tests: `./mvnw test` (from `/home/daniel/sandbox`).
- Run just the acceptance test: `./mvnw test -Dtest=AcceptanceTest`.
- Full build: `./mvnw verify` or `./mvnw clean install`.

Because DTOs and mappers are generated at build time, after editing `openapi.yml` or mappers you must rebuild (`./mvnw compile`/`test`) to regenerate `OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto`.

**Key takeaway for edits:** the address value transformation the `AcceptanceTest` expects (trim/collapse to single spaces, uppercase, expand `st`→`STREET`, `ave`→`AVENUE`) does not exist yet. The natural place to add it is `ValidateOwnerFields.service(...)` (normalize `request.setAddress(...)` before the blank check, or make the blank check run post-normalize), so the normalized value flows through `EnsureHouseholdUnique`, `BuildOwner`/save, and the `GET` response. Household comparison already normalizes case/whitespace independently in `EnsureHouseholdUnique`/`AssignHouseholdId`.

